---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const faqs = [
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'When will the native macOS / Apple Silicon version be released on Steam?',
    answer: 'Developer NoShadow officially confirmed on Steam discussions that the native macOS client is code-complete and currently undergoing mandatory Apple notarization and review. Once finalized by Apple, the macOS version will be unlocked on Steam as a free platform update for all Early Access owners.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'What is included in Early Access Build 25128670, and how does it compare to Patreon tests?',
    answer: 'The public Steam Early Access release (Build 25128670, launched September 4, 2026) delivers the complete Act I experience: handcrafted Zalesye overworld sectors, procedural Soviet bunker complexes, 10 factions (6 interactive in Act I), 25+ firearms, 300+ attachment modifications, and dynamic Mist anomalies. It expands significantly upon the Patreon v0.5.117 testing baseline with refined AI detection curves, balanced trader stocks, and locked $19 entry pricing.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'Why doesn\'t my character\'s appearance change when equipping different armor?',
    answer: 'In Early Access Build 25128670, character pixel art sprites do not dynamically change when equipping various body armor vests or combat helmets. While your defensive damage reduction stats apply accurately in the inventory status tab, visible armor paper-doll cosmetics are a confirmed work-in-progress scheduled for future Early Access content patches.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'Why is the default camera FOV so tight, and can I adjust visibility or zoom?',
    answer: 'The default camera in Scavland is intentionally locked at a close isometric perspective to foster claustrophobic tension and tactical vulnerability in dense post-Soviet ruins. While there is no wide birds-eye zoom slider, you can dramatically expand your forward visual field by holding Aim-Down-Sights (Right Click), using scoped weapons, or boosting environmental brightness and outline contrast in the Video settings menu.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'How do I fast-loot containers and transfer item stacks quickly in the inventory UI?',
    answer: 'You do not need to drag items individually between loot containers and your backpack. Holding [Shift + Left Click] on any item or ammunition stack instantly moves it into your active inventory. This fast-loot shortcut cuts your stationary looting exposure by 80%, keeping you mobile in contested hot zones.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'How do I tell friendly NPCs and neutral traders apart from hostile raiders?',
    answer: 'Friendly settlement guards and neutral scavengers remain holstered, give audible verbal warnings if you sprint too close to their perimeter, and display white or faction-aligned overhead markers. Hostile bandits, rogue deserters, and vultures will immediately shout aggressive combat barks, ready firearms, and display red target reticles upon detecting line-of-sight.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'How do weapon jams work and how do I clear a misfire in combat?',
    answer: 'Weapons with durability below 50% have a progressive chance to jam during automatic or rapid fire. If your gun jams, double-tap the reload key [R] or manually cycle the bolt to eject the stuck cartridge and chamber a fresh round. Apply Gun Cleaning Oil or visit a safehouse workbench to restore durability above 70% for zero jam risk.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'How punishing is the death penalty and what happens when you die?',
    answer: 'Scavland employs an unforgiving corpse-run system: dying in the wasteland drops your equipped backpack and held weapons at the coordinates of defeat. However, all items safely stored in your underground Safehouse Stash, faction reputation ranks, and journal progression are 100% preserved. You can equip backup gear and mount a recovery run to loot your fallen corpse.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'How do you survive the toxic Mist and farm rare artifacts?',
    answer: 'Entering the Mist requires a Gas Mask with active filter charge and Anti-Rad medicine. Equip the handheld Anomaly Scanner on hotkey [3] and listen to the audio ping frequency—the faster and higher-pitched the beeping, the closer you are to a high-tier artifact spawned within the anomaly field.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'Is melee combat viable, or do you have to use firearms?',
    answer: 'Developer Lucasmml clarified that pure melee builds are not viable against mutated wildlife and armed raiders. Knives and crowbars are intended solely for stealth takedowns or emergency self-defense when ammunition is exhausted. Firearm ballistics, cover positioning, and jam maintenance are mandatory for survival.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'Is Scavland a rogue-lite or permadeath game?',
    answer: 'No. Scavland is a persistent top-down survival RPG with persistent stash and quest progression. While dying in the wasteland drops your equipped backpack at the spot of defeat, you do not lose your base storage or character progress, and you can mount a recovery run to retrieve your dropped backpack.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'Will Scavland have co-op or multiplayer support?',
    answer: 'At Early Access launch on September 4, 2026, Scavland is strictly single-player to ensure tight ballistics, AI tension, and atmospheric immersion. However, developer NoShadow has officially confirmed that a 2-player cooperative (Co-op) multiplayer mode is on the post-launch development roadmap for the full v1.0 release.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'Can I play Scavland on Steam Deck or with a controller?',
    answer: 'Yes. Scavland is verified for 60 FPS performance on Steam Deck with native twin-stick controller mapping, customizable UI text scaling for 7-inch/8-inch screens, and full gamepad support alongside traditional mouse/keyboard controls.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'Does Scavland support Ultrawide monitors (21:9 / 32:9)?',
    answer: 'Scavland natively renders at 16:9 and 16:10 aspect ratios (fully verified for Steam Deck 800p). Ultrawide 21:9 support is currently in experimental testing; players on ultrawide monitors can run in bordered letterbox mode with crisp pixel scaling at launch.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'What is the official version baseline, and is hotfix v0.5.121 verified?',
    answer: 'The official public baseline on Steam is Early Access Launch Build 25128670. Reports of build v0.5.121 circulating in community chats reflect unverified private tier mentions or internal staging hotfixes. Our wiki team tracks all developer commits; only public SteamDB-verified patches and official NoShadow announcements are published as confirmed changelogs.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Equipment & Economy',
    question: 'Which junk items are most valuable to keep for traders?',
    answer: 'Not all junk is equal. Settlement merchants pay significantly higher barter prices for functional industrial parts such as spark plugs, lighters, toolboxes, electrical relays, and medical supplies compared to common scrap.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Equipment & Economy',
    question: 'What are the best starter weapons for a new player?',
    answer: 'For your first runs, the Makarov PM (low weight backup), TOZ-34 shotgun (instant mutant knockdown in tight corridors), and standard AK-74M provide the most dependable balance of cheap ammunition availability and stopping power.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Equipment & Economy',
    question: 'Will there be weapon modding and ammo unloading?',
    answer: 'Yes. The full game features 25+ base firearms and over 300 attachments. Developer Lucasmml confirmed dedicated weapon modding stations, item repairs, and stack-aware vertical ammo unloading are actively in the development roadmap.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Factions & Quests',
    question: 'Can faction choices lock me out of certain merchants?',
    answer: 'Yes. Zalesye features 10 dynamic factions. Raising reputation with military Bunker Wardens or Scientists unlocks high-tier armor and optical scopes, but attacking their patrols or doing rival contracts can turn them permanently hostile (reconcilable via diplomat Raisa).'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'Is there a cooking system in Scavland, and how do food and hunger work?',
    answer: 'No. Scavland does not feature a culinary cooking mini-game or raw meat cooking mechanics. Hunger and nutrition are sustained by pre-packaged military rations, canned stew (Tushonka), and dried jerky scavenged from wasteland cupboards. However, campfires serve a crucial survival purpose: you must boil contaminated water bottles at a campfire to produce clean drinking water, and resting near a campfire provides passive health regeneration (added in Patch v0.5.169).'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'How do you counter and kill the Tongue Monsters (Lickers)?',
    answer: 'Tongue Monsters are lethal ambush predators that target scavengers with an 8-meter grapple tongue whip. To defeat them, never fight in open fields where they can dodge laterally. Retreat immediately through a narrow doorway or stairwell to break line-of-sight. When the monster enters the doorway bottleneck, its grapple cannot angle around the frame—fire two rapid shots of 12-Gauge Buckshot or heavy 7.62mm rounds to stagger and eliminate it.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'What is the Core Detector / Anomaly Scanner bug, and how do I fix it?',
    answer: 'Some players encounter an edge case where the Anomaly Scanner (Core Detector on hotkey [3]) stops emitting audio pings or fails to register nearby artifact fields after loading a quicksave. To resolve this without restarting your game, holster the scanner, switch to your primary firearm, fire one unsuppressed shot or cycle the bolt, and then re-equip the scanner. This resets the audio spatial listener component.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'How do I use controller hover inspect on Steam Deck and gamepads?',
    answer: 'When playing with a gamepad or Steam Deck, item tooltips can be inspected by holding [Right Bumper / RB] or clicking the Right Analog Stick [R3] over any inventory tile. This locks the cursor on the item card, displaying durability condition, attachment compatibility, and caliber requirements without requiring a mouse.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Release & Platforms',
    question: 'What did the v0.5.169 Day One Patch change in the game balance?',
    answer: 'Update v0.5.169 significantly softened the early game difficulty curve based on community feedback. It introduced the optional Explorer Mode (retains equipped gear on death, autosaves, and doubles quest rewards), activated passive health regeneration at campfires, doubled base player stamina and safehouse stash capacity, reduced weapon jam probability and gear wear rates, and added medical blueprints for dehydration recovery.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Community & Codes',
    question: 'Are there any official Scavland promo codes or cheat commands?',
    answer: 'No official cheat codes or promo gift codes exist for the Early Access launch. Any third-party sites advertising code generators or free item unlockers are unverified.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Equipment & Economy',
    question: 'Why are merchants offering 50% less rubles when I sell weapons or loot?',
    answer: 'In Scavland, merchants enforce strict item specialization. Selling items outside a trader\'s designated category—such as offering firearms to Physician Anna or bringing medical supplies to Gunsmith Petar—imposes an automatic 50% price cut penalty. Always sort your loot: sell guns to Petar, medical items to Anna, mutant trophies to Nadja, and industrial electronics to Anatoly to maximize ruble returns.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Equipment & Economy',
    question: 'Where is Gunsmith Petar located after the v0.5.169 update?',
    answer: 'Following Patch v0.5.169, Gunsmith Petar was relocated from his previous remote station on the southern settlement perimeter directly into the central Zalesye market square, immediately adjacent to trader Grigory\'s workshop. This eliminates long travel times when repairing weapons and buying weapon maintenance tools.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Factions & Quests',
    question: 'How do I safely complete the Corpse Bearer contract without getting ambushed?',
    answer: 'The \'Corpse Bearer\' logistics contract features a scripted bandit ambush triggered upon interacting with the stranded transport wagon. Do not rush straight to the loot. Approach via the elevated rocky ridge overlooking the road, scan the tree line for 3 concealed Bandit Marksmen, and eliminate them with suppressed rifle fire before retrieving the courier package. Smoke grenades provide vital emergency cover if pinned down.'
  },
  {
    category: 'Gameplay & Mechanics',
    question: 'Where is the second player stash unlocked in Patch v0.5.169?',
    answer: 'Patch v0.5.169 unlocked a second permanent player stash locker inside the Crossroads outpost bunker annex, right next to trader Volodymyr. This forward stash shares the same 100% death loss immunity as your primary Zalesye safehouse locker, allowing you to stockpile weapons, ammunition, and medical kits deeper in the wasteland.'
  }
];

const schemaData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  'mainEntity': faqs.map(faq => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    'name': faq.question,
    'acceptedAnswer': {
      '@type': 'Answer',
      'text': faq.answer
    }
  }))
};
---
<Layout 
  title="Scavland FAQ: Release Date, Gameplay Mechanics, Scanner & Loot" 
  description="Comprehensive answers to top community questions for Scavland: Early Access release date, Anomaly Scanner usage, death mechanics, trader items, weapon modding, and mod support." 
  canonical="/faq/"
>
  <Fragment slot="schema">
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schemaData)} />
  </Fragment>

  <section class="listing">
    <p class="eyebrow">Evidence-based answers</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Frequently Asked Questions<span style="color:var(--acid)">.</span></h1>
    <p class="lede" style="max-width:720px;margin-bottom:2.5rem;color:var(--muted)">
      Everything you need to know about Scavland's September 4, 2026 Early Access launch, core survival mechanics, developer-confirmed systems, and wasteland extraction.
    </p>

    <div class="prose faq-list">
      {faqs.map((faq, index) => (
        <details open={index < 4} style="margin-bottom:1.25rem;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.08);background:rgba(255,255,255,0.02);border-radius:6px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;">
          <summary style="cursor:pointer;font-weight:600;font-size:1.1rem;color:var(--heading,#fff);list-style:none;display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center;">
            <span>{faq.question}</span>
            <span style="font-size:0.75rem;padding:0.2rem 0.5rem;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(218,255,125,0.1);color:var(--acid,#daff7d);font-family:var(--font-mono,monospace);">{faq.category}</span>
          </summary>
          <p style="margin-top:0.75rem;margin-bottom:0;color:var(--text-muted,#c5c5c5);line-height:1.6;">
            {faq.answer}
          </p>
        </details>
      ))}
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top:3rem;padding:1.5rem;border-left:3px solid var(--acid,#daff7d);background:rgba(218,255,125,0.05);border-radius:0 6px 6px 0;">
      <h3 style="margin-top:0;font-size:1.1rem;">Have a question not listed here?</h3>
      <p style="margin-bottom:0.75rem;color:var(--text-muted,#bbb);">
        Check out our comprehensive field guides for in-depth breakdowns on weapons, maps, factions, and survival routes.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/guide/">Browse All Field Guides <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
